**Findings (7)**

1. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/assets/membership.md:129` — **medium**. The sequence is declared "identical in every one of them" — plan, execute, doctor, verify — but the new step 3 checks a cloned submodule out at `origin/<branch>`'s **remote tip**, which is ahead of the gitlink the base records whenever the pointer lags (the normal state). For a non-init command that means `/vwf:plan` surveys code the base does not pin, and the base's `git status` shows the member as `modified (new commits)` with nothing to commit it — so the base's next `code:merge:develop` refuses on the dirty tree. The tip checkout is right for init (which commits the moved gitlink); the other four commands need the branch at the recorded commit, or the step needs to be scoped to init. The step also uses init vocabulary ("deferred row", "shaping skipped") that plan/execute/doctor have no counterpart for — `execute` in particular halts on an absent member, so what it does with a diverged one is undefined.

2. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:724` — **medium**. The base stages only "every member path whose recorded commit moved because that member committed earlier in the run". A member cloned this run at the remote tip has already moved the gitlink before any commit — and commits nothing when it is already shaped (a second developer cloning the base and running `/vwf:setup`, the common case) or on a **leave it** answer. That gitlink is then neither staged nor committed: the base commits, the report says shaped, and the tree is left with a modified gitlink the merge tasks refuse. Membership's "the gitlink moving forward is the expected outcome" only holds if (b) stages every cloned member's pointer, moved or committed.

3. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:710` (with `:815` row 1 and `:41-54`) — **medium**. An existing repo with an **unborn HEAD** — `git init` then `/vwf:setup`, no commits yet — falls between the two paths: it "already exists" so §1 does not create it on `develop`, and it "has no commits" so the (b)/(d) branch work is skipped; `git symbolic-ref -q HEAD` answers `refs/heads/master` (or `main`), so it is not refused as detached either. Row 1 then applies literally: the ops commit lands on `master`, `main` is created from HEAD, and `develop` — which row 1 assumes §1 already produced — is never created and never checked out. The merge tasks and doctor (c) fail afterwards. The fix is one line: on an unborn HEAD, point HEAD at `develop` (`git symbolic-ref HEAD refs/heads/develop`) before the commit.

4. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:803` (and `existing-repo.md:1243`) — **low**. The remote-tracking rule reads `origin/develop` / `origin/main` without a `git fetch` first, and an existing local `develop` is checked out as it stands. On a checkout whose remote-tracking refs or local `develop` are stale — any clone that has sat a while — the ops commit lands behind the remote and (e)'s push is rejected; (e) now handles that as a deferral, but its own text says the case "should not arise", and one fetch before (d) would make that true.

5. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:340-351` — **low**. §7's header still counts "**Nine**" positions, "three are repo-level", and "the seven that sit in the toolchain manager's config and task files", while the same section now says the splice "reaches all ten" and numbers the pair fourth/fifth/sixth (four repo-level, eight in the toolchain files). Doctor (e) splices "every marked position init's `new-repo.md` enumerates"; an implementer counting from the header drops one of the landing pair and reports a filled `MERGE_MODEL_MAIN` as content drift.

6. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:51-54` — **low**. §1 still says §11 creates the missing branch "after the commit question, so the branch work reads against a tree this run has already written to". (b)/(d) now do the branch work and the `develop` checkout **before** staging and before the commit question on a repo with commits. A reader following §1's ordering commits on the branch the repo stood on — the exact outcome decision 3 retires.

7. `/Users/virajpatel/Projects/github.com/virajp/claude-plugins/.worktrees/2026-09-20-branch-model/plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/existing-repo.md:1243` — **low**. The `develop` checkout on an existing repo happens before (c)'s consent is asked, so a **leave it** answer still leaves the repo switched from `main` to `develop` with the run's files dirty on it. Consistent with decision 3 as written, but the plan row for such a repo should say the branch switch happens regardless of the commit answer; today only the report does.

No issues in the shell delta: `_scripts/merge`'s per-destination `case` with the legacy fallback and `direct` default is `set -u`-safe and only reached with `develop`/`main`; the git-workflow `read_env` snippet's `^export MERGE_MODEL=` anchor cannot match the `_DEVELOP`/`_MAIN` keys and mirrors the script's fallback order; doctor (f)/(g), the forge-pass require-PR rule and CONTRIBUTING agree with the pack's `direct`/`pr` defaults; the six-position counts in the mise skill, `conventions.md` and doctor (f) are consistent with each other.

Restated:
- `plugins/vwf/assets/membership.md:129` — tip checkout applies to plan/execute/doctor/verify too: surveyed code ≠ pinned commit, base gitlink dirty, merge refuses
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:724` — base stages gitlinks only for members that committed; a cloned-at-tip member that commits nothing leaves the base dirty
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:710` — existing repo with unborn HEAD (`git init` + setup) commits on `master`/`main`, `develop` never created
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:803` — no fetch before reading remote-tracking branches; stale refs make the "should not arise" rejected push routine
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:340` — §7 header still counts nine / three repo-level / seven in toolchain files vs ten below
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/new-repo.md:51` — §1 says branches are created after the commit question; (b)/(d) now do it before
- `plugins/vwf/skills/init/references/existing-repo.md:1243` — `develop` checkout precedes the commit consent; a leave-it answer still switches the branch, unstated in the plan row
